# run-level-readers.allow — the adjudication half of scripts/run-level-reader-census.sh
#
# One row per file that BOTH reaches a workflow-run feed (gh run list / gh run
# view / .workflow_runs[] / actions/runs) AND reads a conclusion off it.
#
#   <path> <run-level-reference-count> <VERDICT> <reason>
#
# The count is per FILE, never a line number: line-anchored pins slide on
# insertion and red naming files the diff never touched. Adding a reference to an
# adjudicated file changes the count and reds; moving code inside it does not.
#
# VERDICTS
#   RUN-LEVEL        answers a question from the workflow-RUN conclusion. This is
#                    the hazard: continue-on-error makes a red job roll up green,
#                    so the answer is a true green about the wrong object.
#   JOB-LEVEL        the run feed is only an index; the verdict is read from jobs
#                    or check-runs, which is the honest level.
#   KNOWS-THE-CLASS  reads the run conclusion AND explicitly models the rollup.
#   HARNESS          a .test.sh; its matches are fixtures for the script it tests.
#   PROSE            the only matches are message or error strings.
#   CENSUS           this census itself: its matches are its own scan patterns and
#                    its own selftest fixtures. Adjudicated rather than excluded -
#                    an exclusion is a blind spot written into the instrument.
#
# RUN-LEVEL rows are ENUMERATED, NOT FAILED. This is a census: it establishes who
# reads what and makes that impossible to leave un-updated. Changing any reader's
# behaviour is separate work with its own row.

.github/workflows/deploy.yml 6 RUN-LEVEL anchors its path-diff base to `gh run list --status=success` (line 68); a run whose deploy job was continue-on-error red still advances the base, silently dropping that push's paths. The SIXTH reference (task-0c3069135d1b4bfd) is the `convergence` job, and it is JOB-LEVEL by construction: it reads `actions/runs/<id>/jobs` for the control-plane and instance legs' `.started_at` and NOTHING else -- a CLOCK, never a conclusion -- to date the cutoff past which a merged commit is not yet owed a deploy. There is no verdict for a run rollup to launder. It cannot regress into a run-level read either: the value is consumed as `--owed-before <ISO>`, so a `.conclusion` substituted there is not a date and the check refuses with HARNESS-UNAVAILABLE rather than passing. Note also this file carries NO continue-on-error anywhere, stated in report-deploy-failure's own comment, so the laundering shape the class is named for has no producer here
scripts/crown-reconcile.sh 8 RUN-LEVEL filters the deploy population with `select(.conclusion == "success")` over .workflow_runs[]; a partially-failed deploy run counts as a success to reconcile against. The fifth reference is the dead-trigger check (dr-w35): an ANY-STATUS in-window run count over .workflow_runs[] that deliberately reads NO conclusion - the presence of a run, not its verdict, is what proves the push trigger alive. THREE MORE ARRIVED WITH THE WATERMARK (task-7a85d1b5f471af8f), and NONE of them turns a run-level fact into a green: one reads `.status != "completed"` over .workflow_runs[] to build the set of runs that were still IN FLIGHT when the run list was sampled, and two read `.workflow_runs[]?.id` alone - max and min - with no conclusion and no status at all, because Actions allocates run ids in creation order and that ordering is how the script tells a run that did not yet EXIST from one that is genuinely absent. The status read can only ever make the verdict DECLINE TO JUDGE a crown row (printed as WRITTEN-IN-FLIGHT, excluded from both sides, judged normally by the next run and capped at SERVING_INFLIGHT_CAP_SECONDS so a hung run is accused instead); it can never turn a red into a pass, and the load-bearing run-level lie in this file remains the `.conclusion == "success"` filter already adjudicated above
scripts/registration-sample.sh 1 RUN-LEVEL reads `.workflow_runs[] | [.path, .status, .conclusion]` (line 217) and answers per-workflow status from the run rollup, not from check-runs
scripts/pds-pull-proof.sh 2 RUN-LEVEL reports the last deploy from `gh run list --json headSha,conclusion` (line 569); advisory output, but it is the run conclusion being shown as the deploy verdict
scripts/main-gate-watch.sh 2 KNOWS-THE-CLASS reads repos/<r>/actions/runs only to ENUMERATE, then asserts at check-run level; its header states the class verbatim - "`gh run list` itself launders the red (a run whose Sobelow job concluded `failure` reads `success` at the RUN level)"
scripts/release-scan.sh 5 KNOWS-THE-CLASS reads .workflow_runs[].conclusion and models the rollup explicitly, printing "its check suite rolled up green, so GitHub excluded it: continue-on-error" as a first-class case
scripts/absent-context-census.sh 10 JOB-LEVEL reads .workflow_runs[] for {id, path, status, run_attempt} only - never .conclusion - then descends to actions/runs/<id>/jobs for the verdict
scripts/absent-context-census.test.sh 17 HARNESS fixtures for absent-context-census.sh. The three new references arrived with the not-yet-created-job fix: the age guard (D1C, UNDISPATCHED_YOUNG), the needs:-gated pair (D4C DISPATCHED_PENDING / D4D NAME_NOT_IN_RUN), and the both-limbs queue fixture (D10) -- four fixtures added, one removed with the old D4B in_progress mutation, net +3. Every one is a `jq` REWRITE of a captured .workflow_runs[] payload fed back through --fixtures; the fields they set are .status, .created_at, .run_attempt and .id, and NOT ONE of them reads .conclusion. The assertions that follow are on absent-context-census.sh's own class and VERDICT output, which the row above adjudicates JOB-LEVEL. So the count moves and the verdict does not -- 2026-09-01, +5 with the orphan/dormancy split (section 5c): a proved orphan, the same tuple on a LIVE head, a DISPATCHED tuple, the liveness-unreadable fail-closed arm, and the dormant-PR flip. Re-read before the count was moved: every one is the SAME shape as the rows above -- a `jq` rewrite of the captured .workflow_runs[] payload fed back through --fixtures, setting .created_at, .updated_at and .head_sha, plus new jobs-<id>.json and main-head.json fixtures. MEASURED: zero of the five read .conclusion. The assertions that follow are on the script's own class and VERDICT output, which the row above adjudicates JOB-LEVEL. So the count moves and the verdict does not.
scripts/registration-sample.test.sh 1 HARNESS fixtures for registration-sample.sh
scripts/release-scan.test.sh 4 HARNESS fixtures for release-scan.sh
scripts/stale-verdict-watch.test.sh 2 HARNESS fixtures for stale-verdict-watch.sh
scripts/check-deploy-smoke.sh 1 PROSE the single match is an error string quoting deploy.yml's anchor
scripts/check-deployyml-filters.sh 1 PROSE the single match is an error string quoting deploy.yml's anchor
scripts/run-level-reader-census.sh 8 CENSUS its own SRC_RE/READ_RE patterns and the readers its --selftest plants; adjudicated, never excluded from its own walk
scripts/ci-measure.sh 6 JOB-LEVEL the CI measurement harness (task-ee3fc32d1615bd58): reads repos/<r>/actions/runs only to ENUMERATE run ids for a window (lines 291-305), then descends to /runs/<id>/jobs and counts per-JOB conclusions (line 149, 308-309); it answers nothing pass/fail, it tallies job-minutes and reds for the CI-diet report. Lines 330-331 are fixture rows for its own selftest.
scripts/main-red-breaker.sh 1 JOB-LEVEL the main-red circuit breaker (#15740): reads repos/<r>/actions/workflows/<wf>/runs?branch=main&status=completed only to find the NEWEST main run id, then descends to /runs/<id>/jobs and compares per-STEP conclusions of the same-named job with this job's own step outcomes. It never answers from a run conclusion; an unreadable main makes it LESS forgiving (exit 1).
